WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.000
The Pivoting Blind Mate Coupling, or P B M C, defines plug

2
00:00:04.019 --> 00:00:06.740
and socket interfaces for a blind-mate fluid connection.

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.580
The specification describes pivoting behavior that supports the permitted alignment relationship.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.340
It is not inherently limited to one rack frame.

5
00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.760
The animation uses the source drawings and staged highlights.

6
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.760
It identifies the plug and socket, the pivoting compliance and the defined

7
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:23.100
mate-distance relationship.

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.260
It does not invent internal sealing stages, an audible click or a

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:28.920
universal self-centering mechanism.

10
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.160
The specification leaves relevant internal design choices to suppliers while establishing interface

11
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.320
and performance requirements.

12
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:41.120
Evaluate the selected coupling against its permitted mate distances, misalignment, forces, fluid

13
00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.660
conditions and qualification.

14
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.760
A blind-mate label doesn't promise perfect alignment, zero leakage under every condition

15
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.500
or unrestricted live replacement.

16
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.240
Those claims require scoped evidence and approved system procedures.

17
00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:58.020
The correct mental model is a specified interface operating within demonstrated limits,

18
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.200
integrated into a supported mechanical and hydraulic system.

